<h1>Airless Paint Sprayer Cleaning - Magnum</h1>
<div class="row">
	<div class="col-md-4 order-last">
		<div class="card">
			<span class="h4">Also see</span>
			<ul class="list-unstyled">
				<li><a href="@Url.Action("TroubleShooting", "airless")">Airless Paint Sprayer trouble-shooting</a></li>
				<li><a href="@Url.Action("SurfacePrep", "airless")">Surface Preparation</a></li>
				<li><a href="@Url.Action("MagnumParts", "airless")">Magnum Parts</a></li>
				<li><a href="@Url.Action("Repair", "airless")">Sprayer Repair</a></li>
			</ul>
		</div>
		
	</div>
	<div class="col-md-12 order-first">
		<p>Cleansing your airless paint sprayer properly and after every spray job is of the utmost importance! Proper care and maintenance is what is going to make your paint sprayer last and work for you trouble free. Probably half our repair work to sprayers is due to lack of and/or unsatisfactory cleaning. </p>
	</div>
	<div class="col-sm-12">
		<div class="card">
			<div class="card-header">
				<h3>Shutdown and Cleaning Instructions</h3>
			</div>
			<div class="card-body">
				<p>These washing instructions apply to only the Graco Magnum series airless paint sprayers.</p>
				<div class="card">
					<p>See:<a href="@Url.Action("Cleaning", "airless")"> How to Clean a Graco Airless Paint Sprayer</a></p>
				</div>
				<p>If spraying lacquers, purchase <a href="~/store/magnum-lacquer-kit">Lacquer Conversion Kit 248202</a>. Follow Shutdown and Cleaning procedures for oil-based materials.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="card-header">
				<h4 class="bold"><a name="Pail_Flushing">Pail Flushing</a></h4>
			</div>
			<div class="card-body">
				<ul>
					<li>For short term shutdown periods (overnight to one week) refer to Short Term Storage.</li>
					<li>For flushing after spraying oil-based coatings, use compatible oil-based flushing fluid or mineral spirits. Read Priming, Oil-based or Water-based Materials.</li>
					<li>For flushing after spraying water-based coatings, use water. Read Priming, Oil or Water-based Materials, or Power Flush.</li>
				</ul>
				<ol>
					<li>Turn power switch OFF. Lift suction tube and prime tube from paint pail. Let them drain into paint for a while.</li>
					<li>Place suction tube in pail filled with flushing fluid and place prime tube in waste pail. </li>
					<li>Turn Spray-Prime/Drain Valve to PRIME.</li>
					<li>Turn Pressure Control knob to the left (counter-clockwise) to minimum pressure.</li>
					<li>Trigger airless gun into waste pail to relieve pressure in hose.</li>
					<li>Remove tip and guard assembly from spray gun and place in flushing fluid.</li>
					<li>Turn power switch ON.</li>
					<li>Slowly align arrow on sprayer with Pail symbol on Pressure Control knob until pump starts. </li>
					<li>Flush until approximately 1/3 of the flushing fluid is emptied from the pail.</li>
					<li>Turn power switch OFF. Turn Spray-Prime/Drain valve to SPRAY.</li>
					<li>To preserve paint in hose, trigger spray gun into paint pail to expel the remaining paint.</li>
					<li>Turn power switch ON. Continue to trigger spray gun until you see flushing fluid starting to come out of gun nozzle. Release trigger.</li>
					<li>Move airless spray gun to waste pail and trigger it to flush pump, hose and airless gun into waste pail. Continue until remaining flushing fluid is gone from flushing fluid pail. </li>
					<li><strong>Fill unit with <a href="~/store/graco-pump-armor-quart">Pump Armor</a>&#153; storage fluid</strong>. Read Long Term Storage.</li>
				</ol>
			</div>
			<div class="card-header">
				<h4 class="bold"><a name="Power_Flush">Power Flush</a></h4>
			</div>
			<div class="card-body">
				<p>Power flushing is a faster method of flushing. It can only be used after spraying <b>water-based</b> coatings.</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Turn power switch OFF. Lift suction tube and prime tube from paint pail. Let them drain into paint for a while.</li>
					<li>Place suction and prime tube in waste pail.</li>
					<li>Turn Spray-Prime/Drain Valve to PRIME.</li>
					<li>Turn Pressure Control knob to the left (counter-clockwise) to minimum pressure.</li>
					<li>Trigger spray gun into waste pail to relieve pressure in hose.</li>
					<li>Remove tip and guard assembly from spray gun and place in flushing fluid.</li>
					<li>Screw power flush attachment to garden hose. Open valve.</li>
					<li>Turn on water. Rinse paint off suction tube, prime tube and inlet screen.</li>
					<li>Turn lever to close power flush attachment.</li>
					<li>Unscrew inlet screen from suction tube. Place inlet screen in waste pail.</li>
					<li>Connect garden hose to suction tube with Power Flush attachment. Leave prime tube in waste pail.</li>
					<li>Turn Spray-Prime/Drain valve to SPRAY.</li>
					<li>Align arrow on sprayer with pail symbol on Pressure Control knob until pump starts.</li>
					<li>
						Open lever on Power Flush attachment.
						<p>Step 15 is for returning paint in hose back to paint pail. One 50-ft (15-m) hose holds approximately 1-quart (1-liter) of paint.</p>
					</li>
					<li>
						<ol>
							<li>Pull and hold spray gun trigger. Point gun into paint pail.</li>
							<li>Turn power switch ON to begin pumping paint in hose back into paint pail.</li>
							<li>When water comes out of gun, continue to trigger gun, aiming gun into waste pail.</li>
						</ol>
					</li>
					<li>Continue triggering airless spray gun into waste pail for 1-2 minutes, until relatively clear water comes out of gun.</li>
					<li>Turn Spray-Prime/Drain valve to PRIME.</li>
					<li>Circulate water through sprayer, into waste pail, for 20 seconds.</li>
					<li>Turn power switch OFF.</li>
					<li>Close Power Flush attachment. Turn off garden hose.</li>
					<li>Unscrew Power Flush attachment from suction tube.</li>
					<li><strong>Fill unit with <a href="~/store/graco-pump-armor-quart">Pump Armor</a>&#153; storage fluid</strong>. Read Long Term Storage.</li>
				</ol>
			</div>
			<div class="card-header">
				<h4 class="bold">Cleaning InstaClean&#153; Fluid Filter <i>(XR, ProX models)</i></h4>
			</div>
			<div class="card-body">
				<p>The InstaClean Fluid Filter prevents particles from entering paint hose. After each use, remove and clean it to insure peak performance.</p>
				<ol>
					<li>Turn power switch OFF.</li>
					<li>
						Disconnect airless spray hose from sprayer and remove InstaClean Fluid Filter.
						<br> InstaClean filter Then, unscrew outlet fitting First, unscrew hose
					</li>
					<li>Check InstaClean Fluid Filter for debris. If needed, clean filter with water and a soft brush.</li>
					<li>
						Install InstaClean Fluid Filter.
						<br>Install open end of InstaClean filter in outlet fitting, then screw outlet fitting into sprayer outlet fitting
					</li>
					<li>Tighten outlet fitting and reconnect hose to sprayer.</li>
				</ol>
			</div>
			<div class="card-header">
				<h4 class="bold">Airless Spray Gun Fluid Filter</h4>
			</div>
			<div class="card-body">
				<p>Clean sprayer gun fluid filter with compatible solvent and a brush every time you flush the system. Replace airless gun filter when damaged.</p>
				<p>If you want to see some pictures of paint sprayers that have not been taken care of, see The <a href="@Url.Action("WallOfShame", "airless")">Airless Wall of Shame</a>.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>